  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0157 database is designed to manage a library's collection and operations. It contains 17 tables that work together to store information about countries, publishers, book languages, book statuses, customers, books, book inventory, storage locations, loans, authors, and various logs. The country table stores information about different countries, with each country having a unique identifier and a name. The category table contains categories of books, while the publisher table stores details about the publishers of the books. The book_language table lists the languages in which books are written, and the book_status table tracks the status of each book. The customer table holds information about the library's patrons, including their name, date of birth, and contact details. The book table stores details about each book, including its title, publication date, and language, and links to the publisher and language tables. The book_inventory table tracks the availability of each book, including its status and storage location. The storage_location table stores the shelf and section where each book is kept. The loan table records when a book is borrowed, including the customer who borrowed it and the due date. The author table contains information about the authors of the books, and the book_author table links authors to the books they have written. The book_category table links books to their categories. The book_return table tracks when a book is returned, and the log_statement, log_loan, and log_deleted_book_return tables store logs of various events, such as user queries and book returns.",
  "gold_question": "Library Management System\n\n 1) Background / Context\nThe project involves developing a library management system using a MySQL database. This system is designed to manage various components of a library, including book inventories, authors, customers, and the process of lending and returning books.\n\n 2) Objectives\n- To provide an efficient system for managing library resources.\n- To track and manage book loans and returns.\n- To maintain accurate records of books, authors, customers, and transactions.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Library Staff: Responsible for managing inventories, handling loans, and overseeing returns.\n- Library Members/Customers: Individuals who borrow books from the library.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- Book Management: \n  - Store detailed information about books, including title, publication date, language, and publisher.\n  - Classify books by categories and track their availability using the Book Inventory and Book Status tables.\n\n- Author Management:\n  - Record author details, including nationality, using the Author and Country tables.\n  - Map relationships between books and authors.\n\n- Customer Management:\n  - Maintain member information, including contact details and date of birth.\n\n- Loan Management:\n  - Track book loans with details on loan and due dates.\n  - Manage returns and record the return date.\n\n- Inventory Tracking:\n  - Maintain records of book locations within the library using the Storage Location table.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Security: Ensure data privacy and secure access to system functionalities.\n- Performance: The system should efficiently handle data queries and transactions.\n- Scalability: The system should be scalable to accommodate an increasing number of books and library members.\n- Logging:\n  - Maintain logs for loan transactions and deleted book return records for auditing purposes.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0157.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0157\nCREATE TABLE `country` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `category` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `publisher` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_language` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `language` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_status` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date NOT NULL,\n  `contact_details` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `publication_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `publisher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `language_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`publisher_id`) REFERENCES `publisher` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`language_id`) REFERENCES `book_language` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_inventory` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `storage_location_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_inventory_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_inventory_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`status_id`) REFERENCES `book_status` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_inventory_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`storage_location_id`) REFERENCES `storage_location` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `storage_location` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `shelf` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `section` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `loan` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `due_date` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `loan_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `loan_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `author` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_author` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `author_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`, `author_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_author_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_author_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`author_id`) REFERENCES `author` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_category` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`, `category_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_category_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_category_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`category_id`) REFERENCES `category` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_return` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `loan_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `return_date` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_return_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`loan_id`) REFERENCES `loan` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `log_statement` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `log_message` text NOT NULL,\n  `log_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `log_loan` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `loan_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `log_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `log_loan_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`loan_id`) REFERENCES `loan` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `log_deleted_book_return` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_return_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `log_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `log_deleted_book_return_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_return_id`) REFERENCES `book_return` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
